      "narrationText": "Green Tea!\n\n-\n\nRanked!\n\n-\n\nSimple one.\n\n-\n\n0 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n\n-\n\nNo real protein story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real vitamin story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real mineral story here.\n\n-\n\nOn the plus side: catechin content adds real upside. That gives it a useful compound story beyond the near-empty nutrition label. Strong polyphenol reputation. The core appeal of green tea lives in its compounds and effects rather than classic nutrition composition. Nearly zero-calorie daily use. A huge practical advantage in a category judged more by effect than macros.\n\n-\n\nOn the weaker side: taste can be a barrier. Not everyone enjoys it enough to use consistently. Quality varies by source. The practical value depends somewhat on the product. Can be a bit fussier than grab-and-go drinks. A tiny practical downside, but not a serious one.\n\n-\n\nGreen Tea has a genuinely strong overall case. The practical downsides are real, but they do not outweigh the upside. Best treated as a context item rather than a nutritional cornerstone.\n\n-\n\nS tier.\n"
