      "narrationText": "Processed Honey!\n\n-\n\nRanked!\n\n-\n\nSimple one.\n\n-\n\n82.4 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n\n-\n\nNo real protein story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real vitamin story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real mineral story here.\n\n-\n\nThe upsides first: pleasant natural sweetener identity. People value it as a recognisable sweetener rather than as structural nutrition. Easy to use in drinks and foods. Simple practical upside. Familiar and common. That keeps it relevant to score at all.\n\n-\n\nNow the downsides: mostly concentrated sugar. That is the main reason this lands weakly in a context-driven category. Heat processing weakens the case further. Processed honey loses some of the argument raw honey might have made. Overall payoff is weak for misc. The upside does not outweigh the sugar concentration strongly enough.\n\n-\n\nProcessed Honey does have a few real-world upsides. But the nutrition case is still weak and the downsides drag it down hard. Best treated as an occasional context item, not a nutritional base.\n\n-\n\nD tier.\n"
