      "narrationText": "Sports Drink!\n\n-\n\nRanked!\n\n-\n\nSimple one.\n\n-\n\n6 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n\n-\n\nNo real protein story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real vitamin story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real mineral story here.\n\n-\n\nOn the plus side: has a narrow but legitimate sports use case. The category should recognise context when a use case is actually real. Context tells the real story. That is the whole point of misc. Clear real-world role. If a misc item helps or harms behavior, that matters a lot.\n\n-\n\nThe drawbacks next: terrible as a casual everyday drink. Outside hard training, the sugar is hard to justify. Easy to overrate or misuse. This category attracts strong marketing and habits. Rarely deserves to be treated as a foundation food. Most of these are situational, not core nutrition plays.\n\n-\n\nSports Drink does have a few real-world upsides. But the nutrition case is still weak and the downsides drag it down hard. Best treated as an occasional context item, not a nutritional base.\n\n-\n\nD tier.\n"
