        "narrationText": "Cocoa Powder (Unsweetened)!\n\n-\n\nRanked!\n\n-\n\nSimple one.\n\n-\n\n57.9 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n\n-\n\nNo real protein story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real vitamin story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real mineral story here.\n\n-\n\nPros first: shockingly dense on paper. Unsweetened cocoa is one of the rare misc items that actually brings real numbers too. Clear real-world role. If a misc item helps or harms behavior, that matters a lot. Use case can matter more than macros. This category is really about function and trade-offs.\n\n-\n\nNow the downsides: normal serving sizes are much smaller than 100 grams. That trims how much of the paper score you really realise. Easy to oversell beyond what the numbers support. Misc items often attract exaggerated narratives. Better replacements often exist. That practical comparison matters.\n\n-\n\nCocoa Powder (Unsweetened) has a genuinely strong overall case. The practical downsides are real, but they do not outweigh the upside. Best treated as a context item rather than a nutritional cornerstone.\n\n-\n\nA tier.\n"
