        "narrationText": "Coconut Oil!\n\n-\n\nRanked!\n\n-\n\n100 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 82.5 grams, a major pressure point. For this category, the real question is fat quality.\n\n-\n\n0 grams of carbs. Everything else here is pretty flat. Not relevant here.\n\n-\n\n0 grams of protein. The rest of the section is nothing special. Also not relevant here.\n\n-\n\nThe rest of the section is nothing special.\n\n-\n\nMinerals are basically not adding much here.\n\n-\n\nOn the plus side: strong cooking-stability case. Tests whether practical cooking arguments can rescue brutal fat chemistry. Simple ingredient identity. Cleaner than industrial spreads. Strong healthy-food halo. Likely audience argument magnet.\n\n-\n\nOn the weaker side: saturated fat is extreme. This should hammer it hard if the category means what it says. Overall fat profile is weak. Very poor fit for an elite fats ranking. Health reputation can outrun the data. Useful editorial counterweight.\n\n-\n\nCoconut Oil does have a few real-world upsides. But the nutrition case is still weak and the downsides drag it down hard. Best only in small amounts when the cooking job matters more than the nutrition case.\n\n-\n\nD tier.\n"
