        "narrationText": "Dark Chocolate 85%!\n\n-\n\nRanked!\n\n-\n\nSimple one.\n\n-\n\n46 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n\n-\n\nNo real protein story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real vitamin story here.\n\n-\n\nNo real mineral story here.\n\n-\n\nPros first: meaningfully better than typical candy. The misc ranking should reward better swaps, not just raw perfection. Clear real-world role. If a misc item helps or harms behavior, that matters a lot. Can still earn points as a better swap. The category should reward harm reduction when it is real.\n\n-\n\nNow the downsides: still very much a dense treat. It cannot escape being a treat food just because it is darker. Rarely deserves to be treated as a foundation food. Most of these are situational, not core nutrition plays. Better replacements often exist. That practical comparison matters.\n\n-\n\nDark Chocolate 85% does have some solid upside. But the tradeoffs keep it from climbing higher. Best treated as a context item rather than a nutritional cornerstone.\n\n-\n\nB tier.\n"
