        "narrationText": "Lard!\n\n-\n\nRanked!\n\n-\n\n100 grams of fat. Omega 3 is 1000 milligrams, doing a lot of the work here. For this category, the real question is fat quality.\n\n-\n\n0 grams of carbs. Everything else is fairly underwhelming. Not relevant here.\n\n-\n\n0 grams of protein. Outside of that, the profile is pretty quiet. Also not relevant here.\n\n-\n\nOutside of that, the profile is pretty quiet.\n\n-\n\nMinerals are basically not adding much here.\n\n-\n\nOn the plus side: can help meals feel more complete and usable. Fats sometimes improve the whole plate, not just their own stats. Efficient energy source. That can be a strength in the right context. Small amounts can change a whole meal. That leverage matters when the fat quality is good.\n\n-\n\nNow the downsides: easy to overpour without noticing. Practical portion creep is real. Easy to overuse without noticing. Liquid calories are slippery in the kitchen. Calorie density is brutally high. Tiny serving errors matter here.\n\n-\n\nLard does have some solid upside. But the tradeoffs keep it from climbing higher. Best in controlled amounts where fat quality is the main reason to use it.\n\n-\n\nB tier.\n"
